steps.content:
- *Talk to Gertrude in her house west of Varrock. 
*Find and speak to Bob the cat again.
**Bob may be in the same location you previously found him, so check there first.
}}

Items required: a beer or 3 coins.
- *Speak to Burntof in the Rising Sun Inn in Falador.
**If you do not have a beer, buy any beer for 3 coins by talking to Emily or Kaylee. }}

Items required: Gas mask
- *To begin speak to Elena in East Ardougne (directly west of shortcut log).  After a slight delay, you will arrive in West Ardougne.
}}

Items required: The plague sample, touch paper, a priest gown, and an Ardougne teleport (51+ Magic suggested).
- *With your Priest gown equipped head to Guidor's house in the south-east of the fenced area.
*Speak to Guidor, tell him Elena has sent a sample that needs to be processed.  of Ardougne Castle and speak to King Lathas. 
*Congratulations, quest complete!
}}

- *Go to the canal barge north of The Digsite and speak to the barge foreman.
*Speak to the sawmill operator in the Lumber Yard. 
**If you don't have the requirements to enter, just try and open the eastern gate of the guild to complete this step.
*Bring the sawmill agreement back to the Lumber Yard's sawmill operator. 
}}

- *Travel to Port Phasmatys (take a charter ship if you don't have Ectophial).
*Talk to Bill Teach in the inn. 
}}

Items needed: 10 Oak planks (unnoted), 10 steel nails, a hammer and a spade. (Note: Followers are not allowed.)
- *Talk to Larry by the penguin cage in the Ardougne Zoo.  (If talking to Larry with all of the items in your inventory, Larry will automatically take you to the iceberg if you select you are ready)
}}

- *Travel to the dock north-east of Rellekka and speak to Larry
*Left-click Travel back to Rellekka using the nearby boat. 
*Talk to Larry on the dock.
*Read the clockwork book.
}}

- Items needed: A regular plank, a steel bar OR a clockwork mechanism, and a piece of silk, access to a Crafting table 3 or better in a POH.
*Go to your POH and use your Crafting table 3 to turn your steel bar into a clockwork mechanism. 
*Return to Ardougne and talk to Larry. 
*Talk to Larry once on the iceberg. 
}}

Note: while in Meiyerditch if you are provoked by a Vyrewatch you can log out to avoid any interactions with them.
- *Go north-west a short distance (still on the pier), search the floor then kick it down and climb down.
*Climb over the wall rubble and talk to any Meiyerditch citizen. 
*Climb up the ladder in the building south-west of Old Man Ral.
}}

Recommended: Chronicle or combat bracelet (members) with at least 2 charges, amulet of glory (members) with at least 1 charge, Lumbridge teleport (if you need anti-dragon shield)

- *Talk to the Guildmaster in the Champions' Guild. 
*Talk to the Guildmaster in the Champions' Guild. Make sure you get the maze key by asking about Melzar's map piece, and also ask about Thalzar and Lozar's map pieces as well as where to find the right ship. 
*If you don't already have an anti-dragon shield, speak to Duke Horacio on the  of the Lumbridge Castle. 
}}

Items required: Hammer, 3 planks, 90 steel nails, 2,000 coins, Crandor map. Recommended: Amulet of glory (members) with at least 1 charge for teleport to Draynor Village

- *Talk to the Guildmaster and ask him where to find a ship and captain.
*Grab 3 wood planks, 90 steel nails, a hammer, and 2,000 coins out of the bank.
*Talk to Klarense in the southern docks of Port Sarim by the Void Outpost boat and pay him 2,000 coins. 
}}

Items required: 10 eagle feathers, 50 gp, swamp tar, yellow dye.
- *Head to the south-east corner of Varrock to the Fancy Clothes Store (via Varrock tele, Rat Pits Grouping teleport, etc.)
*Talk to Asyff. 
}}

- *Travel to Entrana (speak to monks on second most northern dock in Port Sarim) 
*Talk to Auguste on Entrana north of the Herblore shop (3 times) 
*Go slightly south of Auguste and fill up the sacks with sand.
*Give Auguste a yellow dye, a red dye, ten silk, a bowl, and eight sandbags.
**A bowl spawns in the house east of Auguste on the 
}}

Items required: 3 beers
- *Talk to Commander Veldaban in Keldagrim, just west of the bank. This will begin a cutscene (note: If you click the east side of the bridge directly as the cutscene begins your avatar will migrate east during the cutscene). 
*Speak to the drunken dwarf in the middle of East Keldagrim (north-east of the kebab shop, there's a bar south). 
*Talk to him again and give him a beer. 
}}

Items required: 2 buckets of water, 2 barley malts, kelda hops, empty beer glass, and ale yeast or a pot and 25 coins
- *Go upstairs in the East Keldagrim pub.
*If you did not bring ale yeast, buy ale yeast from Blandebir for 25 coins (empty pot spawn can be found near the vat). }}

- *Talk to the southernmost cart conductor in south-eastern Keldagrim. 
*Return to the minecarts and ride the southernmost cart (no ticket necessary, but need both hands free).
}}

Items required: ghostspeak amulet, bucket of slime (can be purchased during quest)
- *Ask the ghost innkeeper if he has any jobs for you. He'll give you a bedsheet. 
*Ask ghost villagers around town for signatures with the bedsheet equipped. You can alternate between just two ghosts for all the signatures. If one asks you for ecto-tokens, you can ignore them and ask the other, or you can pay if you have tokens to spare. 
*With all 10 signatures, show the petition to Necrovarus.
*Take the key Necrovarus drops and head upstairs. Use the key on the door and enter the room. Take his robes from the coffin.
}}

Items required: mystical robes, book of haricanto, translation manual, and a ghostspeak amulet.
- *Return to the old crone.  Once you've spoken to Necrovarus, you will be able to enter Port Phasmatys freely.
*Enter Port Phasmatys one last time and talk to Velorina.
*Congratulations, quest complete!
}}

- *Talk to Sylas by the POH portal in Taverley. 
*Steal a feather from next to his nest.
*Return to Sylas and give him the feather. 
}}

- *Go to the stone tower south of the Mind Altar.
*Climb over the crumbling wall on the East side (58 Thieving)
*Talk-into to the drain pipe. Then talk into it again 
}}

''(Note: Bring a Summer Pie if boosting Agility for Taverley Dungeon shortcut and an Admiral's Pie if you need to boost Fishing. )thumb|352x352pxItems needed: 1: Vial of water'' and Harralander or Harralander potion (unf), Fishing Rod, Fishing Bait, Dusty Key- *Talk to Gerrant, the fishing shop owner in Port Sarim about lava eels.  Do not ask for a reward.
*Enter the area with the blue dragons, either by using your key on the locked door or take the agility shortcut.
*Run to the southernmost lava pool.
*Catch a lava eel. You only need one, as they cannot be burned. (Catch extra in case you accidentally eat it.)
*Cook the eel on a range or fire.
}}

:Note: If you start the quest with the required/recommended weapons and armour, you will have to bank everything before travelling to Entrana.
- *Talk to King Arthur. 
**He will now be found on the , in the room with the cauldron. Go up the main staircase and head to the eastern room. He won't show up as a yellow dot on the minimap until you have entered the room.
}}

- *Bank all weapons and armour. Travel to Entrana.
*Talk to the High Priest in the chapel. ) or combat bracelet to Ranging Guild.
*Talk to Galahad and receive the holy table napkin. 
**(Talk to Galahad again to complete a task in the Kandarin easy diary )
*Travel to Draynor Manor's  southern-most room with the holy table napkin in your inventory and pick up 2 magic whistles from the table. The whistles will not be visible until you enter the room.
}}

- *Talk to the Wanderer north-east of Sophanem (see picture) and ask why she has a problem with your cat. 
*Touch the door of the pyramid where you wake up.
}}

- *Drop your cat and talk to the Sphinx, ask for help. (if you give the wrong answer your cat will disappear)
*Talk to the High Priest to the south-west.
}}

- *Obtain the black, red, white, and yellow beads:
**Buy them from the Grand Exchange for {{Coins|{{GEP|Red bead|1 +  +  + }}
**Kill imps, recommended for free players either near the southern entrance to Falador or the top of the Karamja volcano; or for members east of the Ardougne Monastery, at the entrance of Chasm of Fire, or around the Charcoal furnace
*Talk to Wizard Mizgog on the top floor of the Wizards' Tower with all four beads in your inventory.
*Congratulations, quest complete!}}

- *Talk to a Legends' Guard east of Ardougne .
*Talk to Radimus. (A machete can be obtained from the cupboards next to Radimus Erkle. Papyrus can be obtained on the table next to him.) 
}}

*Items required: Hammer, saw, 5 mahogany planks, bolt of cloth, cadava berries
*Recommended items: Varrock teleport
- *Talk to the Wise Old Man in Draynor Village.
*Take the Old man's coffin.
}}

Items needed: Weapon and armour to defeat tortured and demonic gorillas, food and prayer potions. Recommended: Slayer ring teleport, an emergency teleport.- *Talk to King Narnode in the Grand Tree.
*Talk to Nieve. If you ever lose Nieve, she will be at the front doors of the Grand Tree.  
*Follow the path to Glough.
*Kill the 2 tortured gorillas and 2 demonic gorillas. It's recommended to kill one tortured gorilla, then the Demonic gorilla that jumps down. Then proceed to kill the other tortured gorilla and demonic gorilla.
*At this point you can safely teleport out and restock. Glough can hit 66 with his melee attack and 40+ with his ranged attack.
}}

- *Speak to King Roald. 
*Climb down the trapdoor just to the north. 
*Kill the Temple Guardian. Players may safespot it by getting it stuck in the middle section of the room against the east wall and standing on the east wall one section north.
}}

''Items required: An eye of newt, a Greenman's ale, a rotten tomato and a dirty blast (ashes added to a fruit blast).
Skills required: 10 Cooking.
- *Speak to the Lumbridge Cook. 
*Enter the door behind the Cook and watch the cutscene.
}}
Note: Many cooking related item requirements can now be bought from the Culinaromancer's chest.''

- *Ask Duke Horacio in Lumbridge Castle for a quest and he'll give you an air talisman. 
*Talk to Aubury south of Varrock east bank in the Varrock rune shop and give him the research package. 
*Take the research notes back to Sedridor.
*Congratulations, quest complete!
}}

- *Talk to Thormac on the top floor of the Sorcerer's Tower south of Seers' Village. )
*Go to Seers Village and speak to a Seer. (Wait until the seer is done checking himself in the mirror.)  Be sure not to skip this step, as the scorpion in Taverley Dungeon is not accessible without first speaking to the seer.
*Scorpions can be caught in any order and there is no need to return between each catch.
}}

{|
|
|
|
|}

- *Make two Serum 207 by adding clean tarromin to a vial of water and then adding ashes.
*Use one dose on Razmire (afflicted) in the general store. 
}}

- *Talk to Father Reen outside Al Kharid bank. ) and go north-east.
*Talk to Father Badden near the ruin entrance.  Be sure to have Silverlight in your inventory.
*Pick and use a black mushroom (or black dye) on Silverlight to dye it black (you can find some beside the staircase).
*Go down the stairs and grab a copy of the Strange implement in the north-west corner of the ruin.
*Talk to Evil Dave in the dungeon wearing your 3 black items and your dyed Silverlight. 
}}

- *Talk to Father Badden outside.
*Convince Father Reen to join the ritual. 
*Use the Strange implement on the golem to reprogram him.
*Talk to the golem again to make him enter the dungeon.
}}

Note: The quest will not be officially started until you have used the wampum belt on Trufitus.

- *With one free inventory space, talk to Mosol Rei outside of Shilo Village. A gnome glider is nearby, as well as fairy ring {{Fairycode|CKR. 
*Use the wampum belt on Trufitus, found in the most north-eastern house in Tai Bwo Wannai (quest icon on minimap). Fairy ring  is nearby.
*Follow the chat options once you've used the belt on him. 
}}

Recommended: Food, potions, and combat equipment. Protect from Melee can be used to negate all damage during this section.
- *Speak with Elena in the Rehnison household basement hideout to start The Battle of West Ardougne.
*Defeat the 15 Knights of Ardougne and Paladins in the castle. (some are upstairs)
*Speak to King Lathas. 
*Watch the cutscene to its completion
}}

Items recommended: Iorwerth camp teleport, teleport crystal, combat gear, food, potions (drink 1 dose of antidote++ before leaving Lletya to save inventory space).
- *Speak with Elena near the pond.
}}

- *Talk to Baxtorian to receive a clue scroll. and run east, 76 Agility OR Zul-andra teleport OR charter a ship to Port Tyras and run South East)
*Dig outside the south gates of Prifddinas (Iorwerth camp teleport)
*Spin outside the western entry to the Underground Pass with nothing equipped (Teleport Crystal to Lletya).
*Bank now if you did not bring combat gear
}}

- * Go back to Wizard Persten in Al Kharid (Recommend exiting the abyss via Fire Altar, will place you just east of Persten) and accept the teleport to the Wizards' Tower. 
* Speak with the three apprentice wizards on the  of the wizards tower, Apprentice Felix, Tamara, and Cordelia, in no particular order and view their riddles.
* Speak to Traiborn, and answer 11 when prompted. 
* Speak to Archmage Sedridor or Wizard Persten in the basement. 
}}

- *Speak to Captain Tock just south of the entrance to Falador farm. 
*Upon arrival to Corsair, make sure to speak with Ithoi the Navigator first or else the other npc chats will not work correctly. Find Ithoi by travelling west along the beach. Climb the stairs of the southernmost building on the beach. }}
thumb|375px|Dig here to find the Demonic Doll.

- *Go to the Exam Centre.
*Ask an examiner about an exam. 
**(Optional) Steal a cup of tea from the tea stall if you don't have one already. (This is a Varrock easy diary requirement)
*Go back to the Exam Centre and talk to an examiner. The chat options do not matter; you will fail the exam regardless.
}}

- *Return to an examiner.  – You should receive 'Level 2 Certificate'
*Talk to all 3 students – the female student will demand an opal (can be obtained by panning). Talk to her two times.
*Return to an examiner for the final exam.  – You should receive 'Level 3 Certificate'
**Save all of your certificates to hand in to Curator Haig Halen at the Varrock Museum in exchange for a fruit blast, a required item for Recipe for Disaster subquest Another Cook's Quest or a chocolate cake.
}}

- *Prepare for battle and talk to the Menaphite Leader (just outside the tent).
*Kill the Tough Guy (level 75) (safespot behind bush). He drops a willow blackjack.
*Talk to a villager. 
*Congratulations, quest complete!
}}

- *Talk to Lady Vulcana Lovakengj in the Lovakengj Assembly building to the west of the southern bank. (Xeric's Talisman, Xeric's Inferno) 
** If he tells you to talk to the "Fiery lass" Talk to Ignisia just to the north east, before returning to him. 
}}

Items required: Silly jester hat, silly jester top, silly jester tights, silly jester boots
- *Quick travel to Neitiznot via Maria Gunnars on the docks next to Mord.
*Remove anything from your weapon and shield slots and put on the Jester outfit (hat, boots, tights, top)
*Speak with Slug Hemligssen north of the bank. ,
}}

- *Teleport to Camelot or walk to Seers' Village.
*If you are making the lyre yourself:
**Spin the golden fleece into a ball of golden wool while in Seers' Village (upstairs in a house south-west of the bank).
**Use the golden wool on your unstrung lyre.
*Go to the Seers' Village pub and talk to the Poison Salesman to buy a low alcohol keg for 250 coins. 
}}

- *The glider will crash near the Ship Yard. Run east past the level 53 jogres to the Ship Yard gate.
*Open the gate and tell the worker Glough sent you, then give the password Ka-Lu-Min. 
*Take the lumber order to the king. (Teleport into the stronghold or get Femi to sneak you in, costing 1,000 coins if you didn't help her earlier). The king will not believe you when you show him the lumber order.
}}

- *Travel to Brimhaven and talk to Sandy.
**Select an option until you distract him, and use the truth serum on Sandy's Coffee Mug. 
}}

- *Head back to the mine cart. Put Ana in the mine cart, then take the cart yourself. 
}}
: Do not remove clothes to go to jail. If you do, you will have to mine 15 rocks to get out.
- *Head back to the surface.
*Operate the winch (south-west in the camp), then search the barrel west of the winch to find Ana. (Do not go through the gate)
*Put Ana on the wooden cart at the centre of the Camp.
*Talk to the mine cart driver. 
*Head back to Irena for your reward.
*Congratulations, quest complete!
}}

- *Talk to King Bolren in Tree Gnome Village. Accept the quest and you will be taken out of the maze and placed at the north-west corner. 
*Talk to him again to give him 6 logs.
*Then talk to him a third time. 
}}

- Items Required: Climbing boots.
*Talk to Ug in the south-west corner of the Troll Stronghold's middle level. Offer him your help. 
*Talk to Ug again.
}}

- Items Required: rope, maple or yew logs, iron bar, swamp tar, bucket of wax, cake tin.
*Talk to Tenzing in the hut west of the Warriors' Guild in Burthorpe. 
*Talk to him again to get the sled. 
*Use the swamp tar on the bucket of wax to get Wax.
*Use the Wax on your Sled.
}}

- * Speak to Ennius or Furia Tullus outside the Sunrise Palace. 
* Head down the stairs into the temple crypt.
* Head north through the gate and talk to Prince Itzla Arkan and Servius, Teokan of Ralos.
* Return to Ennius and Furia inside the Sunrise Palace, in the green area by the entrance, to receive a Varlamore crest.
}}

Items required: 20 unnoted rune essence or pure essence (Must all be the same type), Commorb.
- *Talk to the Mage of Zamorak  if Temple of the Eye is completed.) in Varrock at the  Altar of Chaos.
**If you have not yet started the Enter the Abyss miniquest, you must first talk to him in the Wilderness north-east of Edgeville. He will then tell you to talk to him in Varrock.
*Speak to him again to give him the 20 rune or pure essence. 
}}

- * Speak to Ivy Sophista in Taverley, in the building where the crystal chest is found.  and launch an arrow towards you; swap to Protect from Melee after the arrow lands, and then focus back on the assassin.
** Note that there is currently a small glitch where the player may not be able to attack the second assassin, so let Thaerisk kill him off if this occurs. Thaerisk cannot die during this fight.
* Finish the conversation with Thaerisk.
}}
